# Slurm Scheduler ({{ title }})

All real computation on {{ title }} runs as **Slurm** jobs. Never run compute on a login
node (see `unix.md`) — submit it here.

{% if scheduler.require_qos %}
## Every {{ title }} job needs four things

A job request must specify **resources**, an **account**, a **QOS**, and a
**partition**. On {{ title }} you MUST explicitly set **both the account
(`-A`/`--account=`) and the partition (`-p`/`--partition=`)**; also set the QOS
(`-q`/`--qos=`) and always a time limit (`--time`).
{% else %}
## Every {{ title }} job needs three things

A job request must specify **resources**, an **account**, and a **partition**. On
{{ title }} you MUST explicitly set **both the account (`-A`/`--account=`) and the
partition (`-p`/`--partition=`)**, and always a time limit (`--time`).
{% endif %}

- Discover the accounts you can {% if charging %}charge (and their balances){% else %}submit to{% endif %} with **`{{ commands.accounts }}`** — do not
  guess an account name.
- Set a realistic `--time`; memory is allocated in proportion to the cores you request.

