## QOS{% if charging %} and charging{% endif +%}

{% if 'normal' in qos %}
- **`normal`** — the default; normal priority, charged against your account.
{% endif %}
{% if 'standby' in qos %}
- **`standby`** — access to idle resources at low priority, **not charged**, max {{ scheduler.standby_max_hours }}
  hours. Request it with **`-q standby`** (it is a QOS, **not** an account).
{% endif %}
{% if 'preemptible' in qos %}
- **`preemptible`** — `ai` partition only; cheaper GPU-hours, but jobs can be preempted
  (killed) to make room for `normal` jobs — checkpoint your work.
{% endif %}
{% if 'training' in qos %}
- **`training`** — required for the `training` partition (`-q training`); low priority,
  **not charged**, max 24 hours.
{% endif %}
{% for q in qos if q is mapping %}
- **`{{ q.name }}`** — {{ q.text }}
{% endfor %}
{% endif %}

## Common commands

`sbatch` (submit a batch script), `squeue -u $USER` (your jobs), `scontrol show job
<id>` (job detail), `scontrol hold`/`release`, `scancel <id>` (cancel), `{{ commands.interactive }}`
(interactive job), `srun` (launch tasks).
{% if commands.job_helpers %}

RCAC helpers: `jobinfo <id>` (one view of a running or finished job, from `sacct`, `sstat`
and `squeue`), `jobscript <id>` (the job's submission script), `jobcmd <id>` (its
submission command line), `jobenv <id>` (its environment).
{% endif %}

## Prohibitions

{% for ap in anti_patterns %}
- {{ ap }}
{% endfor %}
{% if 'standby' in qos %}
- **Do NOT** write `-A standby` or `#SBATCH -A standby` — `standby` is a QOS
  (`-q standby`), not an account.
{% endif %}
- **Do NOT** emit flags for other schedulers (PBS/Torque `#PBS`, LSF `#BSUB`) — this is
  Slurm.
- **Do NOT** invent {% if qos %}partition or QOS names; the valid sets are{% else %}partition names; the valid partitions are{% endif %} listed above.
- **Do NOT** submit jobs without a `--time` limit, and **do NOT** `scancel` jobs you do
  not own or run bulk cancellations without confirming with the user.
